{title: Watch Answering Watch}
{subtitle: Ezra 8:24; Nehemiah 10:11; 3:17; 11:15–22; 12:24–26}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 70}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Dm] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
At the Ahava ca[Eb]nal we stood [Bb]
Twelve leaders [Gm]set a[F]part by hand [Bb]
Silver and [Gm]gold in our [Bb]care
For the [Eb]house of the living [Gm]God
We [Eb]carried the vessels of [Fsus4]praise
To re[F]store the broken [Bb]altar
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Watch answer[Eb]ing watch we [Bb]stay
Praise and [Gm]thanks in [F]day and [Eb]night
Following [Bb]David the man of [F]God
[Gm]Keeping the covenant [Eb]tight
Hashabiah leads the [F]song
In the rhythm of the [Bb]Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Beside Rehum we made repairs
Ruler of half the district
[Gm]Building the wall stone by stone
In the [Eb]service of His spirit
We [Bb]sealed the covenant with God
Under [Dm]Nehemiah's care
Our names [Eb]are written in the dust
Bound [F]to the holy air
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Watch an[Bb]swering watch we [Eb]stay
Praise and [Bb]thanks in day [Gm]and night
[F]Follow[Eb]ing David the man [Bb]of God
Keeping the [F]co[Gm]venant tight
Hashabiah [Eb]leads the song
In the rhythm of [F]the Lord
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
In the days of Joia[Bb]kim
[F/A]And the [Gm]priest and scribe Ezra
We kept [Eb]the gates and the store
With [Bb]no pause in our la[F]bor
Serving [Gm]in the work of God
[Eb]From the morning to the eve
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]Watch answering watch we [Eb]stay
In the [Gm]house of the [F][Eb]Lord
{end_of_verse}
